From 5c022088deffe6757028d2e8f351c8473de78837 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 10:57:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: stm32/hash - fix DMA alignment boundary case for
 secured context
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For secured HASH contexts (mp2x and mp13), the first non-final DMA
update must leave data for the next transfer so the hardware context can
be saved safely.

The current guard misses the boundary case where new_len == nbytes.
This happens when the input size is congruent to 4 modulo the block size:
after adding one word, the whole buffer may be consumed in the first
transfer, leaving nothing for the follow-up update and breaking the
save-context invariant.

Use ">=" so one block is also dropped in this case.

Fixes: 3525fe475245 ("crypto: stm32/hash - add full DMA support for stm32mpx")

Change-Id: I94931f59e807d674ce71b5a627a30642af8e1a11
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/587311
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c b/drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c
index 08b51ac7ab7e..68296c6587d8 100644
--- a/drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/stm32/stm32-hash.c
@@ -1173,7 +1173,7 @@ static int stm32_hash_align_sgs(struct scatterlist *sg,
 		 */
 		if (init && secure_ctx) {
 			new_len += sizeof(u32);
-			if (unlikely(new_len > nbytes))
+			if (unlikely(new_len >= nbytes))
 				new_len -= bs;
 		}
 	}
-- 
